            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0919" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123C38/108: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-13T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1919, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 10th noon.</p>
                <p>Department knows of no tug proceeding to Costa Rica. Endeavor to get telegram
                    through to Consul Chase inquiring as to his safety <pb facs="0920" n="818"
                        xml:id="pg818"/> and welfare. Cable Department fullest possible news
                    regarding Acosta’s expedition and again warn [?] authorities in Nicaragua to see
                    there is no just cause of complaint on part of Costa Rica.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
